15:38.583 --> 15:40.482
Masturbator and Commander.

15:42.553 --> 15:44.851
<i>Captain, the enemy ship
has opened fire on us.</i>

15:44.956 --> 15:47.652
<i>I'll be right out.
- Sir, we've already lost 10 men.</i>

15:47.758 --> 15:50.453
<i>- Hang on.
- Sir, don't you think we should return fire?</i>

15:50.560 --> 15:51.653
<i>Yeah, yeah, go ahead and do that,</i>

15:51.762 --> 15:53.820
<i>and I'll meet you up there
in, like, five minutes.</i>

15:53.997 --> 15:56.228
Peter, I've never seen you so happy.

15:56.334 --> 15:59.360
Well, Lois, I never realized
what it was like to have a real dad.

15:59.470 --> 16:01.562
I mean, my own dad
was such a ballbuster,

16:01.671 --> 16:03.866
I guess I just always thought
that was normal.

16:03.974 --> 16:06.101
But Papa Tom is so different.

16:06.209 --> 16:09.645
For the first time in my life, I feel
like I have a real family, you know?

16:09.746 --> 16:12.442
I mean, I'm not just going through
the motions like I do around here.

16:12.549 --> 16:15.073
<i>Hey, champ,
you want to watch Chicken Little?</i>

16:15.651 --> 16:17.745
- Yeah.
- And what does a chicken say?

16:17.854 --> 16:19.150
"Moo. "

16:19.788 --> 16:20.756
Why not?

16:21.324 --> 16:22.291
Come on, Ma.

16:23.158 --> 16:24.490
Hey, what gives with the suitcase?

16:24.594 --> 16:28.586
Tom, there's no easy way to say this.
I'll just come right out with it.

16:28.697 --> 16:31.860
- I'm leaving.
- What? Leaving? Why?

16:31.967 --> 16:33.696
Tommy, this has been great,

16:33.802 --> 16:36.565
but I wasn't looking
for anything long-term.

16:36.671 --> 16:40.233
I just needed someone to clear
all the bats out of my plumbing.

16:40.342 --> 16:42.969
- What do we do now, Bill?
- We write, Tim.

16:43.111 --> 16:44.546
We write our story.

16:45.814 --> 16:47.975
Goodbye, dear.

16:49.418 --> 16:51.181
It's all my fault!

17:01.329 --> 17:04.196
I know it hurts right now, Peter,
but we'll get through this.

17:04.298 --> 17:06.425
- You're still my little buddy, right?
- Yeah.

17:06.534 --> 17:09.935
- Then we'll be okay. Goodnight, buddy.
- Goodnight Papa Tom.

17:10.038 --> 17:12.563
- Goodnight, son. Goodnight, Lois.
- Goodnight.

17:13.042 --> 17:14.702
Peter, this is a little strange.

17:14.809 --> 17:17.369
No stranger than when
Darth Vader was a meter maid.

17:18.413 --> 17:21.973
Come on, man. Cut me a break.
I was only in there for, like, five minutes.

17:22.082 --> 17:23.710
I already started writing the ticket.

17:23.818 --> 17:26.081
You know,
I make your annual salary in a week.

17:26.186 --> 17:28.882
Are you happy doing what you're doing?
'Cause you're pathetic.

17:39.566 --> 17:43.262
I gotta do it, Karen.
I just gotta take a shot.

17:43.369 --> 17:45.668
That guy... That guy just got to me today.

17:45.772 --> 17:48.672
You do whatever you think is right,
and I'll support it.

17:50.444 --> 17:53.571
I don't really understand it.
What do you want this loan for?

17:53.679 --> 17:56.843
I want to build a giant space station
that can destroy a planet.

17:56.950 --> 17:59.714
I don't know that that would be a good
investment on our end.

18:00.152 --> 18:01.847
I mean, I want to open a sports bar.

18:01.954 --> 18:04.582
<i>Good morning, Quahog.</i>

18:04.690 --> 18:06.749
You're here with Dingo...

18:08.060 --> 18:09.492
And the Baby...

18:10.763 --> 18:12.526
And if you're thinking about changing
the station...

18:12.631 --> 18:14.928
<i>Don't you do it!</i>

18:15.033 --> 18:17.525
Today we got homeless Hank
from the dumpster out back with us.

18:17.635 --> 18:18.602
Hey, I got an idea.

18:18.703 --> 18:20.432
How about the first three women
willing to come down

18:20.538 --> 18:24.441
and have sex with Hank get free boob jobs
courtesy of Dr. John Viener?

18:24.543 --> 18:26.806
- Are you reading my mind, man?
- Let's go to the phones.

18:26.911 --> 18:29.779
Go ahead, caller,
you're on with Dingo and the Baby.

18:31.049 --> 18:33.415
<i>Is this Dingo?
- Yes, honey, what's your name?</i>

18:33.518 --> 18:36.111
Sindy, with an "S."

18:36.220 --> 18:39.986
- Hot. Hot.
- Oh, yeah, that's hot, that is hot.

18:40.090 --> 18:41.114
Tell me something, Sindy,

18:41.225 --> 18:43.057
how'd you like to come down here
and get naked for us?

18:43.161 --> 18:44.525
<i>Sure.</i>

18:46.197 --> 18:47.221
I think we got a show.

18:47.332 --> 18:49.800
- Oh, yeah, we got a show.
- We definitely got a show.

18:49.901 --> 18:51.994
Oh, yeah, there's a show.

18:52.103 --> 18:55.094
<i>After all, AIDS is a deadly,
incurable disease.</i>

18:55.205 --> 18:59.403
<i>But no matter how you come to judge
Charles Wheeler and his partners</i>

18:59.510 --> 19:01.909
<i>in ethical, moral, and in human terms,</i>

19:02.011 --> 19:03.206
<i>the fact of the matter is,</i>

19:03.780 --> 19:07.875
<i>when they fired Andrew Beckett
because he had AIDS,</i>

19:07.984 --> 19:10.476
<i>they broke the law.</i>

19:10.587 --> 19:12.885
My God, what is wrong with you?

19:12.990 --> 19:15.082
I swear to God
that was supposed to be "food fight. "

19:18.228 --> 19:21.355
- I want some ice cream.
- No, Peter, you finish your food.

19:22.498 --> 19:25.228
You, hey... You get back here
right now, mister.

19:25.701 --> 19:28.863
Don't you... Get down from that chair
or you're in big trouble.

19:28.970 --> 19:31.633
You put that ice cream back right now.

19:31.741 --> 19:36.111
I mean it. I am not kidding around.
I am not gonna say it again.

19:37.513 --> 19:41.210
If you put that ice cream in your mouth,
you're gonna be in big trouble, young man.

19:48.557 --> 19:52.687
- I hate you, I hate you. I want my mommy.
- Well, I'm the best you've got.

19:53.028 --> 19:54.086
All right, so you know the drill.

19:54.196 --> 19:55.754
We're gonna turn on the hot dog cannon,

19:55.864 --> 19:57.992
and for every hot dog
that you catch in your mouth,

19:58.100 --> 20:01.535
you get $100 toward a boob job
that you desperately need.

20:01.636 --> 20:04.264
- I know.
- Okay, here we go.

20:04.873 --> 20:06.363
A miss.

20:06.708 --> 20:08.607
You got her in the eye with that one.

20:08.709 --> 20:11.270
That one was a teat-seeking missile.

20:11.379 --> 20:14.211
I'm looking for Brian Griffin.

20:14.315 --> 20:18.615
<i>- Gore Vidal?
- I was supposed to do The Lunch Hour.</i>

20:19.486 --> 20:23.150
<i>- This is The Lunch Hour.
That one felt like my dad.</i>

20:23.258 --> 20:26.249
<i>Incest in the morning.
Suppressed memories.</i>

20:26.360 --> 20:27.918
<i>97. 1.</i>

20:28.028 --> 20:30.292
I think I may have made a mistake.

20:30.397 --> 20:33.264
No, no, no, no, this is it.
You're in the right place.

20:33.367 --> 20:36.029
Listen, why don't you
stick around and talk for a while.

20:36.136 --> 20:38.070
My listeners would love to hear
about your new book.

20:38.172 --> 20:41.901
$100, boob job!
- I'm gonna go.

20:43.042 --> 20:44.907
Oh, my God, what have I done?

20:45.011 --> 20:47.276
Hey, it's all about ratings, baby,
and we got 'em.

20:47.381 --> 20:51.408
No, it wasn't worth it.
I'm sorry, Stewie, I can't do this anymore.

20:51.518 --> 20:54.611
I'm more of a sellout than you were when
you did those Butterfinger commercials.

20:55.322 --> 20:58.290
Nobody better lay a finger
on my Butterfinger.

21:02.195 --> 21:05.630
- What's your problem?
- Papa Tom's being a jerk.

21:05.731 --> 21:07.062
At least he talks to you.

21:07.165 --> 21:10.192
He's my dad and he hasn't
paid attention to me in weeks.

21:10.303 --> 21:11.964
Well, all in all, you should be thankful.

21:12.071 --> 21:15.199
I think the Kennedys had a kid like you,
and they had it put to sleep.

21:15.308 --> 21:17.936
Hey, Peter, I'm sorry about that business
with the ice cream.

21:18.044 --> 21:21.206
I guess I'm just still a little torn up
about your mom.

21:21.346 --> 21:23.177
But, hey, I'll make it up to you.
Let's play catch.

21:23.282 --> 21:24.249
Okay.

21:27.685 --> 21:29.347
Wait a minute. You know what?

21:29.454 --> 21:31.887
- I think you should play catch with Jake.
- Really?

21:31.989 --> 21:35.017
Yeah, I had a taste of what it was like
to have a real father.

21:35.128 --> 21:37.061
I can't make him share his.

21:37.162 --> 21:39.596
Well, all right, Peter. Come on, Jake.

21:40.531 --> 21:43.865
I guess I've learned a little something
about what it means to be a good dad.

21:43.969 --> 21:45.833
Hey, Dad, do you want to play baseball?

21:45.936 --> 21:49.702
Oh, my God, could you leave me alone?
You are the neediest kid.

21:50.308 --> 21:53.765
- I can't believe you gave up our show.
- Yeah, sorry.

21:53.877 --> 21:56.039
I wonder who they got to replace us.

21:56.847 --> 22:00.647
- It's magic hour with Dark Chocolate...
- And the Rod.

22:00.751 --> 22:03.879
<i>In Rod we trust.
97. 1.</i>

22:04.522 --> 22:05.887
<i>Giggity Giggity Goo.</i>

22:05.888 --> 23:06.888
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru